      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "For the same circle-theta observable, the source gives two nested explanations for weak or absent zero signatures: the explicit -√τ₂ correction decays more slowly than the zero-indexed powers and can mask them, while the inverse-Mellin Eisenstein calculation sharpens masking to exact decoupling by giving Cρ(R)=(1/2πi)R^(-ρ/2)[ζ*(ρ)]²=0. Zero locations may belong to the general transform without being visible in every observable.",
