      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_8cadff11c055e4c33b1c7e40e77960aa5d8bc13289b8999a8ae0e4443bee65a3",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The rational SO(8) presentation turns the Scherk-Schwarz spectrum into parity-controlled signed coefficients, and the later proper-time sum uses those same coefficients to compare microscopic boson-fermion alternation with a vacuum-energy trend and an RH-conditional zero-frequency residual. This provides a model-level calibration of the proposed spectral error structure, not an independent test of the Riemann hypothesis.",
